/P 225 0 R
/T (Yom Haasmaut Graciously sponsored by  Bobby & Elaine Dweck)
/E (Yom Haasmaut Graciously sponsored by  Bobby & Elaine Dweck)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (In commemoration of Yom Hazikaron, we took part in a meaningful soldier memorial event at Binyanei HaUmah. The following morning, we joined thousands of Israelis on Mount Herzl Military Cemetery to mourn the lives of those that were lost defending our country. It was particularly meaningful to be with the families of fallen soldiers and to hear their stories. Several days later, our students returned to Har Herzl Military Cemetery, where they walked through its many sections, spanning from those who fell in the War of Independence to the present day. For those who are Kohanim and could not attend, Ezra Dweck taught a shiur on Hilkhot Kohanim.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
