<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 228 0 R
/T (After that, we see Eldad and Medad remain behind in the camp, where they received their own prophecy from Hashem. Even though they were separate from the others, they still had an important purpose and role. So again, why am I mentioning all of these different roles and responsibilities? Because this shows us that everyone has a role and purpose in why they are alive. We see from all of these appointed jobs that every person was chosen for something specific.)
/E (After that, we see Eldad and Medad remain behind in the camp, where they received their own prophecy from Hashem. Even though they were separate from the others, they still had an important purpose and role. So again, why am I mentioning all of these different roles and responsibilities? Because this shows us that everyone has a role and purpose in why they are alive. We see from all of these appointed jobs that every person was chosen for something specific.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 228 0 R
/T (It is clear from the parasha that not everyone is meant to do the same thing. Every person serves Hashem in a different way, with different strengths, talents, and responsibilities. Some people lead, some help others, some teach, and some inspire. Yet every role matters. Hashem wakes us up every day so that we can serve Him and live a life of Torah and mitzvot. The different roles in the parasha teach us that every person is unique and special. Everyone has a part in this world and a reason why Hashem put them here.)
/E (It is clear from the parasha that not everyone is meant to do the same thing. Every person serves Hashem in a different way, with different strengths, talents, and responsibilities. Some people lead, some help others, some teach, and some inspire. Yet every role matters. Hashem wakes us up every day so that we can serve Him and live a life of Torah and mitzvot. The different roles in the parasha teach us that every person is unique and special. Everyone has a part in this world and a reason why Hashem put them here.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
