449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 229 0 R
/T (There is something in the air in Eres Yisrael that you cannot find anywhere else in the world. I've been here many times before, but nothing compares to actually living here. The moment you step off the plane, you feel it. A warmth, a pull, a sense that this is exactly where you are supposed to be. It's something you can only understand by being here.)
/E (There is something in the air in Eres Yisrael that you cannot find anywhere else in the world. I've been here many times before, but nothing compares to actually living here. The moment you step off the plane, you feel it. A warmth, a pull, a sense that this is exactly where you are supposed to be. It's something you can only understand by being here.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 229 0 R
/T (The Yeshivah takes us on hikes throughout the year, and walking through this land with my own two feet made me understand something I never could have from just a visit. The land has a heartbeat. You feel it beneath you, around you, in the air you breathe. It's unlike anything I've ever experienced, and I don't think I'll ever stop being grateful for the year that I had.)
/E (The Yeshivah takes us on hikes throughout the year, and walking through this land with my own two feet made me understand something I never could have from just a visit. The land has a heartbeat. You feel it beneath you, around you, in the air you breathe. It's unlike anything I've ever experienced, and I don't think I'll ever stop being grateful for the year that I had.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 229 0 R
/T (Some of my favorite memories are the simplest ones. Across the street from us is Gan Saker, a park where we'd play frisbee, go for runs, and just be together. One night after night seder, we brought a speaker to the park and started playing Hebrew music. Everyone was laughing and having a good time, and I thought: I cannot believe this is my life right now. That moment is one I will carry forever.)
/E (Some of my favorite memories are the simplest ones. Across the street from us is Gan Saker, a park where we'd play frisbee, go for runs, and just be together. One night after night seder, we brought a speaker to the park and started playing Hebrew music. Everyone was laughing and having a good time, and I thought: I cannot believe this is my life right now. That moment is one I will carry forever.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 229 0 R
/T (Then there was a morning in Rabbi Gold's Gemara class, somewhere around Hanukkah. This year we learned Kiddushin, and I looked over at my friend, and we just smiled at each other. We smiled because we both realized how lucky we are to be learning Torah in Eres Yisrael, from incredible rabbis. I don't think either of us could stop smiling for the rest of the day.)
/E (Then there was a morning in Rabbi Gold's Gemara class, somewhere around Hanukkah. This year we learned Kiddushin, and I looked over at my friend, and we just smiled at each other. We smiled because we both realized how lucky we are to be learning Torah in Eres Yisrael, from incredible rabbis. I don't think either of us could stop smiling for the rest of the day.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 229 0 R
/T (I came here as one person and I'm leaving another. I know that because when I went home for Pesah, I wanted to continue the habits that I built in school. That might sound small, but for me it was everything. This land, this year, these boys changed me. And no matter where I go from here, Eres Yisrael will always feel like home.)
/E (I came here as one person and I'm leaving another. I know that because when I went home for Pesah, I wanted to continue the habits that I built in school. That might sound small, but for me it was everything. This land, this year, these boys changed me. And no matter where I go from here, Eres Yisrael will always feel like home.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
