496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (MM: How have you seen the school growth from year one, when you sent Robert, to year five when you sent Morris?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (TF: First of all, in terms of size, it literally grew in numbers. Robert was one of just a handful of students that first year. I just love watching the school get bigger over the years. Nothing changed in terms of the feel of the place though, because the one-on-one relationships with the rabbis are still there. I think Morris just got the opportunity to meet more people and meet different people from around the world, which was very nice. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (MM: Did you see a difference between when your kids went to the school and when they came back? )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (TF: Absolutely. They came back with much more of a direction of what they wanted in life. They came back much more focused, much more spiritual, they came home with a love of learning. They were much more independent. Exactly what I would have wanted them to get from their year. Also more religious- each of them for what worked for them. After leaving high school, I don't know how much you love that learning and they came home with a new love of learning. So that was very nice to see them keeping that up. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
