2255 0 obj
<<
/Title (After that, we see Eldad and Medad remain behind in the camp, where they received their own prophecy from Hashem. Even though they were separate from the others, they still had an important purpose and role. So again, why am I mentioning all of these different roles and responsibilities? Because this shows us that everyone has a role and purpose in why they are alive. We see from all of these appointed jobs that every person was chosen for something specific.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2250 0 R
/Next 2261 0 R
>>
endobj
2256 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2250 0 R
/Prev 2262 0 R
>>
endobj
2257 0 obj
<<
/Title (Then there was a morning in Rabbi Gold's Gemara class, somewhere around Hanukkah. This year we learned Kiddushin, and I looked over at my friend, and we just smiled at each other. We smiled because we both realized how lucky we are to be learning Torah in Eres Yisrael, from incredible rabbis. I don't think either of us could stop smiling for the rest of the day.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2219 0 R
/Prev 2251 0 R
/Next 2252 0 R
>>
endobj
