2261 0 obj
<<
/Title (It is clear from the parasha that not everyone is meant to do the same thing. Every person serves Hashem in a different way, with different strengths, talents, and responsibilities. Some people lead, some help others, some teach, and some inspire. Yet every role matters. Hashem wakes us up every day so that we can serve Him and live a life of Torah and mitzvot. The different roles in the parasha teach us that every person is unique and special. Everyone has a part in this world and a reason why Hashem put them here.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2250 0 R
/Prev 2255 0 R
/Next 2262 0 R
>>
endobj
2262 0 obj
<<
/Title (Perashat Behalotekha teaches us many lessons, but one specific lesson is that everyone has a role in why Hashem put them here. We see throughout the parasha how jobs and responsibilities were distributed among so many different people, and that shows us one important idea: every person has a specific role in serving Hashem.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2250 0 R
/Prev 2261 0 R
/Next 2256 0 R
>>
endobj
